Interview Answer (30 Seconds)
====================================================================
"@Service marks a class as a Spring service bean. During component scanning, 
Spring creates an instance of the class and registers it in the IOC container, allowing dependency injection using @Autowired. 
If we don't use @Service or another bean-defining annotation such as @Component, Spring will not create the bean, 
and dependency injection will fail with a NoSuchBeanDefinitionException during application startup."

